    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (82.97) and **Trea Turner** (81.27) serving as our elite offensive anchors. **Yordan Alvarez** draws a favorable matchup against Phillips, where his massive 0.473 xwOBA suggests he is poised to capitalize on the 4.81 xERA projection, making him our highest-scoring start. **Trea Turner** benefits from a distinct tactical advantage; beyond his leadoff spot, he faces a pitcher with a slow delivery, which, when paired with favorable wind conditions, massively inflates his projection for stolen bases\u2014our scarcest category. **Kyle Schwarber** (76.62) rounds out this primary tier, utilizing an ideal #2 order slot and wind conditions to maximize his power output against Wrobleski.\n\nElsewhere, the lineup is bolstered by tactical platoon edges. **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) and **Lars Nootbaar** (64.23) are both high-value starts today, each receiving double-digit percentage boosts from their respective favorable platoon splits against Ure\u00f1a and Avila. While **Dillon Dingler** (58.63) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (58.43) are strong, they carry significant downside risk due to 42% rain probabilities in their venues. **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, in particular, faces a stiff 15% reduction in his score due to an unfavorable platoon matchup against the lefty Valdez, though he remains in the lineup for his elite stolen base potential. The closest call on the bench was the decision to sit our other depth pieces, as **Caleb Durbin** was ultimately removed from consideration due to a confirmed rainout, while **Christian Yelich** and **Colt Keith** remain sidelined. We are keeping a close eye on the weather; if the rain intensifies in the **Dillon Dingler** or **Pete Crow-Armstrong** games, we must be prepared to pivot to any available reserve replacements to protect our daily efficiency.",
